Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:03:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(autostart): escape dynamic values in launchd plists

The plist templates escaped only PATH; Instance, LimaHome, Binary, WorkDir
and UserName went into the XML raw. A path containing & or < then renders a
plist that is not well-formed: plutil rejects it, so launchd will not load it.

Add an xml template function (encoding/xml, rejecting invalid UTF-8 rather
than substituting U+FFFD) and use it for every value in both templates.
ExecuteTemplate now registers the FuncMap, so both plist renderers use it.

Signed-off-by: thc1006 <84045975+thc1006@users.noreply.github.com>
